---
description: >
  Alignment drift after the cold-start install refactor: stale scope path
  and References pointing at moved sibling specs.
intent: >
  scaffoldReadme's scope still names the old path and its References
  section enumerates sibling specs at their pre-move locations.
misalignment:
  - spec-gap
---

## Issues

- [ ] `src/service/install/scaffoldReadme/.aide` frontmatter
  `scope: src/tools/init/scaffoldReadme`
  Stale path — module moved to `src/service/install/scaffoldReadme/`.
  Traces to: physical move; ancestor `.aide/intent.aide` ->
  outcomes.desired[4] (folder tree as architecture).
  Misalignment: spec-gap

- [ ] `src/service/install/scaffoldReadme/.aide` References list:
  every reference points at `src/tools/init/...`
  All four references (`src/tools/init/injectBadge/.aide`,
  `src/tools/init/.aide`, `src/tools/init/writeMethodology/.aide`,
  `src/tools/init/provisionBrain/.aide`) name files that have moved to
  `src/service/install/...`. References are hints not contracts, but a
  reader following them lands on dead paths and has to back-derive the
  current locations.
  Traces to: physical move; ancestor `.aide/intent.aide` ->
  outcomes.undesired[3] (aspirational docs that describe behavior the
  server does not deliver).
  Misalignment: spec-gap

- [ ] `src/service/install/scaffoldReadme/.aide` Strategy: "The parent
  init spec's requirement that every init category have an upgrade path
  applies here."
  The "parent init spec" terminology hardcodes the parent's identity as
  the init tool. After the refactor, the parent is the install service;
  the upgrade-path requirement is correct but scoped to the wrong
  parent identity.
  Traces to: parent `src/service/install/.aide` (currently misaligned —
  this leaf inherits the parent's stale "init tool" framing).
  Misalignment: spec-gap

## Retro

Architectural-shift drift. The References section is the most fragile
part of any moved spec — every wikilink-style path becomes stale on a
rename. A spec-mover would benefit from a sanity check that grep-finds
References lines pointing at the spec's old path.
